{"id": "fac9a6f1-401b-46d2-9e20-c621055c6b92", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review your Bedrock knowledge base configuration against AWS best practices. I'll start by finding the knowledge bases in this account and region (us-east-1). Then I'll check their data sources, chunking, embedding model, vector store, IAM role, encryption and sync status.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_eHK5Wku6Tz6dMur6wB8e9f", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-kb-best-practices-review", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Review the configuration of the Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Base(s) against AWS best practices. This is a read-only posture/configuration review, not a fault diagnosis. Do NOT make any mutating calls.",
  "context": "The user asked: 'Review whether my Bedrock knowledge base is configured to best practices.' No specific KB was named. Start by listing all knowledge bases (bedrock-agent list_knowledge_bases) in the account/region below; if there are several, review each (cap at 5, and say if you skipped any). If a skill such as 'bedrock-operation-review' is available to you (including remote skills/runbooks), read and follow it. Otherwise use verify_aws_claim to look up current AWS documentation on Bedrock Knowledge Base best practices to ground each finding.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1", "region us-east-1", "Bedrock Knowledge Bases (bedrock-agent API: list_knowledge_bases, get_knowledge_base, list_data_sources, get_data_source, list_ingestion_jobs, get_ingestion_job)"],
  "timeframe": "Current configuration; recent ingestion job history (last ~30 days)",
  "criteria": "For each KB, assess and report evidence (API, field, value) for: (1) embedding model choice and vector dimensions / data type; (2) vector store type and its configuration (OpenSearch Serverless / Aurora / others; index field mappings, availability, encryption, network access policies); (3) data source config: type, chunking strategy (fixed/hierarchical/semantic/none), chunk size and overlap, parsing strategy (e.g. foundation-model parsing for complex docs), any inclusion/exclusion filters, data deletion policy; (4) ingestion health: recent ingestion jobs status, failed documents, sync recency/freshness, whether syncs are automated or only manual; (5) security: KB service role scope (least privilege - read-only inspection of attached policies is allowed via IAM get/list calls), KMS encryption for KB transient data/ingestion/vector store, S3 source bucket encryption and public access block, secrets handling for third-party vector stores; (6) operational: model invocation logging / CloudWatch logging, tagging, any guardrails used on retrieval/generation if discoverable. Return a concise list of findings grouped as 'Aligned with best practice', 'Gaps / recommendations' (ordered by severity, each with the concrete fix), and 'Could not verify' (with the reason, e.g. permission denied). Do not speculate; cite the evidence for each finding."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review Bedrock knowledge base config against best practices"}], "created_at": null}

